course: dictionary
lesson: 5670
title: One word, three meanings: liver
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The liver is a large organ inside your body, under your ribs on the right side. It cleans your blood, stores energy for later, and helps you digest food.
explain: «The liver makes bile, which helps to digest fat.» Digest means to break food down so your body can use it. Bile is the liquid that helps your body do this with fat.
explain: The word liver has other meanings too. In «liver and onions», liver means the liver of an animal, cooked and eaten as food. In «a clean liver», it means a person who lives in a certain way, but this meaning is rare.
explain: «Too much paracetamol can seriously damage the liver, even if you feel fine at first.» Context tells you the body part is meant here. Grown-ups keep a note of each dose for this reason.
fact: The liver is the largest organ inside the human body.
fact: The liver removes harmful things from the blood.
fact: The liver stores sugar for energy and makes bile to help digest fat.
fact: «Liver and onions» and «chicken liver» are foods made from an animal's liver.
fact: «Liver disease» means an illness that affects the liver.
exercise: «The liver makes bile, which helps to digest fat.» What job does bile do? | Keeps you warm | *Helps to digest fat | Protects your heart | Makes the blood red
exercise: Where is your liver? | Behind your knees | Under your chin | At the top of your head | *Under your ribs on the right side
exercise: «Too much paracetamol can seriously damage the liver, even if you feel fine at first.» What is the warning? | Medicine always makes the liver bigger | *Too much medicine can harm the liver, even when you feel well | Paracetamol is a kind of food | Only old people need to care about the liver
test: Which organ removes harmful things from the blood? | Lungs | Heart | Stomach | *Liver
test: In «liver and onions», what kind of word is liver? | *A food, the liver of an animal | An action word | A place | A colour
exam: The word liver has more than one meaning. Which meaning is about food? | *The liver of an animal eaten as food | A large organ that stores energy | A part of the brain | A person who lives in a certain way
